# Documented exceptions. Every entry needs a reason and a review date;
# an undocumented suppression is indistinguishable from a cover-up.

# AVD-KSV-01010 - "ConfigMap stores sensitive contents"
# False positive. The flagged keys are PORT ("8000") and GUNICORN_TIMEOUT
# ("120"): a TCP port number and a gunicorn worker timeout in seconds.
# Neither is a credential. The two real secrets, DATABASE_URL and
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, appear in no ConfigMap at all. They are supplied by a
# Secret created imperatively from .env via --from-env-file, so they are
# never written to a file that git tracks.
# Reviewed 2026-11-04, N. Asumadu. Re-review if the ConfigMap gains keys.
AVD-KSV-01010
